1
00:00:00,293 --> 00:00:03,383
(Sheldon:)It's at this point
that you'll wanna start taking notes.

2
00:00:04,797 --> 00:00:07,797
(Sheldon:)Physika means the science
of natural things.

3
00:00:07,967 --> 00:00:11,887
(Sheldon:)And it is there in ancient Greece
that our story begins.

4
00:00:12,305 --> 00:00:14,895
(Penny:)-Ancient Greece?
-Ah. If you have questions, raise your hand.

5
00:00:15,058 --> 00:00:16,638
[CLEARS THROAT]

6
00:00:17,018 --> 00:00:20,358
(Sheldon:)It's a warm summer evening,
circa 600 B.C.

7
00:00:20,521 --> 00:00:24,401
(Sheldon:)You've finished your shopping
at the local market or agora.

8
00:00:28,196 --> 00:00:30,156
(Sheldon:)And you look up at the night sky.

9
00:00:30,323 --> 00:00:33,823
And there you notice
some of the stars seem to move...

10
00:00:33,993 --> 00:00:38,663
(Sheldon:)...so you name them planetes
or wanderer.

11
00:00:45,046 --> 00:00:46,176
(Sheldon:)Yes, Penny?

12
00:00:46,339 --> 00:00:49,049
(Penny:)Does this have anything to do
with Leonard's work?

13
00:00:49,384 --> 00:00:54,434
This is the beginning of a 2600-year
journey we're going to take together...

14
00:00:55,890 --> 00:00:59,350
(Sheldon:)...from the ancient Greeks
through Isaac Newton to Niels Bohr...

